cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ANet-Drone4D in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ANet-Drone4D: A Real-World Grounded 4D World Runtime for Autonomous Multi-Agent Drones"
abstract: >-
  ANet-Drone4D is a real-world grounded digital twin and multi-agent simulation
  platform for drones. It follows one chain, Reality to Reconstruction to World
  to Environment to Simulation to Agent: captured or reconstructed point clouds
  become versioned World Packages with geometry queries, an environment field
  adds wind, turbulence and visibility, a vectorised fleet simulator steps a
  fleet of drones (designed for up to 1,000) on one shared clock, and a browser
  sandbox streams the world progressively while the server computes it. Drones
  are the first kind of physical agent; they discover each other's
  capabilities and delegate tasks through ANet (an in-process mock of the ANet
  network in version 0.1).
